              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The URL you entered\u2014**`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`**\u2014is the legacy (older) website for the Georgia Department of Revenue's Motor Vehicle Division (MVD). \n\nWhile some older links may still redirect you, Georgia has officially transitioned all online motor vehicle, tag, and title services to a newer, unified system called **Georgia DRIVES e-Services**. \n\n### Where to go now:\n* **Official Portal:** [**Georgia DRIVES e-Services** (eservices.drives.ga.gov)](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov/)\n* **General MVD Information:** [Georgia Department of Revenue Motor Vehicles](https://dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles)\n\n---\n\n### Services Available on the Georgia DRIVES Portal:\nUsing the updated portal, you can complete the most common vehicle and tag tasks online:\n* **Tag Renewal:** Renew your license plate registration annually.\n* **Cancel Registration:** Voluntarily cancel your vehicle registration (important to do *before* canceling your auto insurance to avoid fines).\n* **TAVT Calculator:** Estimate the Title Ad Valorem Tax (TAVT) for a newly purchased or transferred vehicle.\n* **Pre-apply for Title/Registration:** Speed up your visit to the county tag office by filling out the paperwork online ahead of time.\n* **Change Address:** Update your address on your vehicle registration.\n* **Pay Insurance Fines / Check Status:** View registration and insurance compliance status or pay active fines.\n\n---\n\n### How to Renew Your Tag Online:\nIf you are trying to renew your license plate registration, make sure you have the following information ready before visiting the portal:\n1. Your **License Plate Number** or **VIN** (Vehicle Identification Number).\n2. Your **Georgia Driver\u2019s License Number** or the **Letter ID/RIN** (Renewal Identification Number) found on your paper renewal notice.\n3. A valid credit/debit card or electronic check to pay the registration and processing fees.\n\n### Alternative Renewal Options:\nIf you prefer not to renew online, you can also:\n* **Use an MV Express Kiosk:** Many grocery stores (like Kroger) and government buildings house self-service kiosks where you can scan your renewal notice, pay, and instantly print your license plate decals.\n* **Visit Your Local County Tag Office:** You can find your specific county's tag office location, hours, and contact info via the [Georgia County Tag Office Directory](https://dor.georgia.gov/county-tag-offices).",
